Next integration owners: vegetation.js should consume biomeAssetRuntimeAdapter without replacing its existing north cryosphere policy; naturalGeology.js should consume geology family/material signals while retaining terrain sampler authority; villages.js should pass architecture candidates through the existing WorldAssetPlacementPipeline; playerRegionalAppearance.js should consume the same distribution policy so player clothing and scenery remain geographically coherent. Keep all four production paths additive and preserve exact-head acceptance gates.

Current QA interpretation:
- The biome policy is canonical geography data, not a replacement terrain or hydrology owner.
- Placement must be evaluated against the live terrain sampler at every candidate point, not only at the regional centre.
- Water proximity, shoreline transition and slope should suppress unsuitable ecology before asset hydration.
- Real authored GLB candidates remain preferred; procedural geometry is fallback, never proof that the authored asset is hydrated.
- Surface fabric must remain world-space and biome-aware so adjacent assets share regional material continuity.
- Near-field assets need higher silhouette fidelity than background scatter; LOD and culling must remain deterministic.
- Settlement assets need terrain grounding and local architecture fit before promotion to a visible landmark.
- North cryosphere assets must not leak into temperate regions merely because a generic vegetation fallback is available.
- Asset selection, placement and material semantics should produce stable digests for identical map/seed inputs.
- A missing texture or GLB should fail readiness explicitly instead of silently masquerading as a successful render.
- Browser visual proof remains necessary after headless contracts pass; contract green is not equivalent to visual realism.
- The next production integration should prefer existing loaders and owners over introducing a parallel asset framework.
- Any integration must preserve road, seat, collider and gameplay ownership boundaries.
- Geometry frequency, density and material contrast should vary with geographic context rather than uniform global noise.
- This file is intentionally a compact continuation ledger; detailed implementation belongs in the canonical world modules and their acceptance scripts.
